\f1\fs22 Chip leapt from the bed which, for a man of his size, meant swinging his legs out like they were lumber, and lowering his feet to the floor. Gingerly, he put on his shoes, then shifted his weight over his ankles as if they were meringue. He cursorily straightened the clothes he had slept in, and left the bedcovers\'97which he had not turned down\'97shaped into a Chip-sized crater.\
He grabbed his device and made a call.\
\'93You have reached John Stoat. If it\'92s less than erudite, please keep it to yourself.\'94\
Chip hung up and sent a text: 
\fs20 STOP! NOW!
\fs22 \
He headed down the hall, past an open door. Without stopping, he said, \'93Morning, Dr Logan,\'94 to the woman sitting on the bed.\
Outside the bunker, on the way to the Ironing Room, he considered how badly the situation might have devolved between factions siding with Eloise or Alexander. Too bad. Whatever weapons they might point at him were firecrackers compared to the machine Stoat was fooling with.
